From 2e4e0b39e5eaa08240a48f33b80b8968286afc23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivel=C3=A4?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:49:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] extensions: let the application say a page is a tab

A page an extension opens with windows.create is a window of its own,
and an application may show it as one of the reader's tabs instead:
Omaweb opens every such page as a tab when the reader has turned Glance
off, and the reader can keep a Glance as a tab. The engine went on
counting the page as the extension's window, so tabs.query listed it
there rather than among the browser's tabs, and the extension could
close the reader's tab with tabs.remove.

QWebEngineExtensionManager::setPageIsTab takes the QWebEnginePage, or
the WebEngineView in Qt Quick, and is invokable from QML. The page
leaves the window it was opened in for the browser's: tabs.query lists
it there, windows.get no longer answers for the window it left, and
tabs.remove refuses it, as it refuses every tab the application keeps.
The extension hears nothing, then or when the page closes. Bitwarden
ends a passkey request when its prompt's window is removed, and the
prompt is still open, now as a tab.

Said while the application is being handed the page, before
windows.create answers, the page is never a window of its own, and the
call answers with the browser's window. The mark lives on the
WebContents, so it holds from before windows.create registers the page,
and dies with it. An extension's own page carries it too, and is then
listed as a tab, where the delegate leaves every other extension page
out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
